title: room.enter
---
<<if $hasLens>>
<<hide mantelLens>>
<<endif>>
<<if not $metToby>>
<<hide mrsHudson>>
<<hide toby>>
The fire is lit. Fog presses at the windows of 221B.
Watson: Nothing in the papers tonight, Holmes. London has gone quiet.
Hero: London is never quiet, Watson. It is only waiting.
<<show mrsHudson>>
<<walk mrsHudson 250 166>>
Mrs Hudson: A young man to see you, Mr Holmes. He's in a dreadful state.
<<show toby>>
<<walk toby 268 170>>
<<walk mrsHudson 298 160>>
<<hide mrsHudson>>
Toby: Mr Holmes? My name is Toby Vance. It's my master, sir. He's gone.
<<set $metToby to true>>
<<else>>
<<hide mrsHudson>>
<<if $tookCase>>
<<hide toby>>
<<endif>>
<<endif>>
===

title: room.look
---
The sitting room at 221B. Books, papers and chemicals, in an order only Holmes understands.
===

title: toby.talk
---
-> Your master?
    Toby: Mr Elias Thorne, sir. Clockmaker, of Clerkenwell. I've been his apprentice three years.
    Toby: He was at his bench when I left last night. This morning the shop was shut up, and he was gone.
    <<set $askedMaster to true>>
-> The door was locked?
    Toby: Bolted, sir, from the inside. I had to fetch the constable to break it in.
    Hero: And the window?
    Toby: Latched. Nobody could have got out that way.
    <<set $askedDoor to true>>
-> The clocks?
    Toby: That's what frightened me, sir. Every clock in the shop had stopped.
    Toby: All at the same minute. Seventeen past three.
    <<set $askedClocks to true>>
-> The lantern?
    Toby: Still burning on the bench when we broke in. He never leaves it lit.
    <<set $askedLantern to true>>
-> We shall go at once. <<if $askedMaster and $askedDoor and $askedClocks and $askedLantern and not $tookCase>>
    Hero: Watson, your hat. Mr Vance, we shall go at once.
    Toby: Thank you, sir. I'll run ahead and open the shop.
    <<walk toby 298 164>>
    <<hide toby>>
    <<set $tookCase to true>>
===

title: toby.look
---
A thin young man in a work coat two sizes too large, turning his cap round and round.
===

title: watson.look
---
Watson, in his armchair, with yesterday's Standard.
===

title: watson.talk
---
<<if $tookCase>>
Watson: I have my revolver, Holmes, if it comes to that.
<<else>>
Watson: The boy is frightened half out of his wits. Hear him out, Holmes.
<<endif>>
===

title: mantelLens.look
---
Holmes's lens, on the mantel where he left it.
===

title: mantelLens.do
---
<<hide mantelLens>>
<<get lens>>
<<set $hasLens to true>>
Hero: Where I go, it goes.
===

title: correspondence.look
---
Unanswered letters, pinned to the mantel with a jack-knife.
===

title: correspondence.do
---
Hero: They have waited a month. They can wait another night.
===

title: violin.look
---
Holmes's violin, laid across a chair. It has seen him through worse evenings.
===

title: bench.look
---
A rack of test tubes on the chemistry bench, and a stain Mrs Hudson has given up on.
===

title: slipper.look
---
The Persian slipper, where Holmes keeps his tobacco.
===

title: fire.look
---
A good fire. The only warm thing in London tonight.
===

title: window.look
---
Fog, thick as wool. The lamps across the street are smudges of yellow.
===

title: door.look
---
The door to the landing, and the seventeen steps down to the street.
===

title: door.do
---
<<if $tookCase and $hasLens>>
<<walk hero 290 162>>
Watson: A cab, Holmes?
Hero: A cab, Watson. Clerkenwell.
<<room 101>>
<<elseif $tookCase>>
Hero: My lens, Watson. I shall want it tonight.
<<else>>
Hero: We have a visitor. It would be rude to leave before he has told us why he came.
<<endif>>
===
